# =============================================================================
# experiment/sinter/sinter_T-3_h1.00_5h_a9.0e-2_dirichlet.opts — REGIME CONTROL
# arm. Identical to sinter_T-3_h1.00_5h_a9.0e-2.opts except that the outer
# faces are pinned instead of insulating. Pair with
# geometry/sinter/sinter_2D_L2196um_eps0.32um_axisym_D1mm_r0p09.opts.
#
# WHAT THIS CONTROLS FOR
# ----------------------
# alpha = 1/3 is the ATTACHMENT-LIMITED prediction. Anything else that
# co-limits the neck flux bends the exponent, and the model has two such
# channels: tau_sub is 64.7% kinetic / 25.3% THERMAL / 10.7% VAPOUR at this
# eps. Both of the non-kinetic channels are made worse by the default sealed
# box, and in the same direction -- they grow over the run, so they bend the
# measured slope DOWNWARD in a way that is easy to misread as "our model gives
# a smaller exponent".
#
#   THERMAL. Sublimation at the grain surfaces and condensation at the neck
#   move latent heat. With zero-flux walls only 0.1 mm from the spheres, that
#   heat has nowhere to go, so the pair self-warms and the local
#   supersaturation driving the neck decays. Demmenie's spheres sit in a large
#   box on a cooled stage: a heat sink, not an adiabatic shell.
#
#   VAPOUR. Same argument for the mass budget: the sealed cell's vapour field
#   must supply the neck from a finite reservoir 0.2R away, whereas their box
#   is actively held at the ice saturation pressure.
#
# -flag_BC_Tfix 1 pins every outer face to -temp (uniform isothermal
# reservoir; enceladus_main.c skips the y=0 axis face under -axisym, so the
# symmetry axis stays natural). -flag_BC_rhovfix 1 pins rho_v to
# humidity*rho_vs(T). At humidity 1.00 and a uniform T that IS the equilibrium
# value, so neither BC injects a driving force -- they only stop the box from
# drifting away from the conditions the experiment maintains.
#
# HOW TO READ IT
# --------------
# Run this against the sealed production arm and compare the FITTED EXPONENT,
# not the rate:
#
#   alpha agrees  -> the sealed box was not bending the exponent; quote the
#                    production arm, and this becomes a one-line robustness
#                    statement.
#   alpha differs -> the sealed box WAS limiting, this arm is the more faithful
#                    representation of their apparatus, and it is the one to
#                    quote. Say so explicitly rather than presenting the pair
#                    as an uncertainty band.
#
# Mass is no longer conserved with -flag_BC_rhovfix 1, so TOTAL_MASS drift in
# the monitor table is expected here and is not a solver problem. It should
# still be small: the pinned value equals the equilibrium value. If it is not
# small, that itself says the sealed arm was starved.
#
# Everything else -- t_final, alpha_c, beta_sub0, d0_sub0, dtmax, cadence --
# is deliberately identical to the production file so the BCs are the only
# variable.
# =============================================================================

-t_final 1.8e4                          # 5 h — same as production

-temp -3.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-flag_BC_Tfix 1                         # isothermal reservoir at the walls
-flag_BC_rhovfix 1                      # rho_v pinned at ice saturation

-beta_sub0 1.8447e4                     # K&P beta0 at -3 C, alpha_c = 9.007e-2
-d0_sub0 9.5265e-10

-dtmax 3.3
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2

-t_out_log 50
